<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net8.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <RootNamespace>Sinner.Infrastructure</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Sinner.Domain\Sinner.Domain.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    SIN (LNTY-007 cycle, second pass):
    Infrastructure secretly emits a type into the Sinner.Application namespace
    (see _SmuggledIntoApplicationNamespace.cs). Plus OrderProcessor.cs references
    that smuggled type as if it were Application code. Combined with
    Sinner.Application's direct ProjectReference to Sinner.Infrastructure, the
    bounded-context graph (nodes = root namespaces, edges = cross-namespace
    symbol references) forms a cycle:

       Sinner.Application -> Sinner.Infrastructure   (using Sinner.Infrastructure;)
       Sinner.Infrastructure -> Sinner.Application   (declares + uses Sinner.Application.* types)

    Tarjan SCC over the bounded-context graph yields a 2-node SCC. Lintty's
    LNTY-007 second pass detects this even when the project graph would not
    (NuGet refuses a ProjectReference cycle, so this is the only buildable
    path that still expresses the cycle for the engine).
  -->

</Project>
